<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Beryl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2024">2024</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Beryl was a powerful Atlantic hurricane of July 2024, the earliest on record to reach Category 5 strength. On 1 July it struck the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a> with winds of about 240 kilometres an hour, destroying most homes on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-island">Union Island</a> and on Grenada's Carriacou. It went on to cause damage in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-beryl.jpg" alt="Hurricane Beryl" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ABI imagery from NOAA's GOES-16 Satellite · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beryl_2024-07-02_1230Z.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
